1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,500
More sources. Where does the answer begin?

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:07,800
Files pile up. Evidence gets scattered.

3
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:11,600
Add documents, images, audio and video to a Space.

4
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:15,400
Parse by format. Keep each source connected.

5
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:20,600
Extract document content, then split it into chunks.

6
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:25,800
Index text by meaning and keywords; retain its source.

7
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:31,000
CLIP turns the image into a visual embedding.

8
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:36,200
Caption the image, then index the description.

9
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:41,400
Transcribe and describe audio, then index the text.

10
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:46,600
CLAP indexes sound alongside the text route.

11
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:52,400
Omni reads visuals and sound to organize scenes.

12
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:58,200
Shots retain descriptions, timing and any transcript.

13
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:04,000
Retrieve mainly by shot; add visual cues as needed.

14
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:09,200
MinIO stores originals and reusable parsed artifacts.

15
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:14,400
Qdrant stores indexes and linked source information.

16
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:18,400
Once parsing and indexing finish, sources can be found.

17
00:01:18,400 --> 00:01:22,000
Start with a question. Look for traceable evidence.

18
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:25,700
A quick lookup, or a question to investigate?

19
00:01:25,700 --> 00:01:29,400
Standard search first interprets your question.

20
00:01:29,400 --> 00:01:34,200
With no library selected, topic profiles guide scope.

21
00:01:34,200 --> 00:01:37,900
Select a library or files to define the search scope.

22
00:01:37,900 --> 00:01:42,700
Auto uses complexity signals to choose a mode.

23
00:01:42,700 --> 00:01:47,700
Direct runs one retrieval round for a quick lookup.

24
00:01:47,700 --> 00:01:52,700
Standard Agent searches in rounds within set limits.

25
00:01:52,700 --> 00:01:57,700
Pi takes its own path and chooses its own tools.

26
00:01:57,700 --> 00:02:02,700
Search, read sources and expand nearby context.

27
00:02:02,700 --> 00:02:07,700
Inspect images, PDF pages or media when needed.

28
00:02:07,700 --> 00:02:11,400
Use the gathered evidence to build a cited answer.

29
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:15,100
Next: how standard search finds relevant evidence.

30
00:02:15,100 --> 00:02:18,900
Standard search selects paths for your question.

31
00:02:18,900 --> 00:02:23,700
Dense retrieval finds text with related meaning.

32
00:02:23,700 --> 00:02:28,500
Sparse retrieval picks up keyword clues.

33
00:02:28,500 --> 00:02:33,300
CLIP matches images by visual meaning.

34
00:02:33,300 --> 00:02:38,100
CLAP matches audio by sound and meaning.

35
00:02:38,100 --> 00:02:42,900
Video search finds relevant shots and moments.

36
00:02:42,900 --> 00:02:47,700
Combine needed paths; not every path runs each time.

37
00:02:47,700 --> 00:02:52,500
Fusion and reranking bring relevant results forward.

38
00:02:52,500 --> 00:02:56,300
Pass selected evidence and source details to the model.

39
00:02:56,300 --> 00:03:00,100
Keep a route back to where the evidence came from.

40
00:03:00,100 --> 00:03:03,900
Numbered citations link answers to their sources.

41
00:03:03,900 --> 00:03:08,700
Open a citation for its file name and excerpt.

42
00:03:08,700 --> 00:03:12,500
Relevance scores rank results; they do not prove claims.

43
00:03:12,500 --> 00:03:17,300
Open the inspector to review the cited material.

44
00:03:17,300 --> 00:03:22,500
Read the passage with available surrounding context.

45
00:03:22,500 --> 00:03:27,700
Open an image preview to check visual details.

46
00:03:27,700 --> 00:03:32,900
Revisit video timestamps or open the audio source.

47
00:03:32,900 --> 00:03:36,700
Compare the answer with text, images or sound.

48
00:03:36,700 --> 00:03:40,500
The link finds the source. You assess the claim.

49
00:03:40,500 --> 00:03:44,300
State what this search found, and where gaps remain.

50
00:03:44,300 --> 00:03:47,800
Before using an answer, check the evidence.

51
00:03:47,800 --> 00:03:51,300
No match this time does not prove absence.

52
00:03:51,300 --> 00:03:54,800
Refine the question or scope, then check again.

53
00:03:54,800 --> 00:03:58,300
Self-hosted for one user on a trusted network.

54
00:03:58,300 --> 00:04:01,800
Offline use depends on models and configuration.

55
00:04:01,800 --> 00:04:07,000
Start with sources. Extract text, visuals and sound.

56
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:12,200
Connect original files, parsed content and indexes.

57
00:04:12,200 --> 00:04:17,400
Follow a query path to gather relevant evidence.

58
00:04:17,400 --> 00:04:22,600
Build the answer from evidence. Keep citations attached.

59
00:04:22,600 --> 00:04:28,800
Return to the source and check what supports the answer.

60
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:31,600
Tessmora

61
00:04:31,600 --> 00:04:35,800
Answers you can trace
